{"created": "2026-10-21T04:48:25.938613+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-21T04:48:27.090258+00:00", "id": 23524358, "conceptrecid": "14019809", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23524358", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.14019809", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23524358", "metadata": {"title": "A Theory of Everything \u2014 Expanded Research Collection: Baird / ZoraASI Corpus, Nielsen Preprint, and Research Supplements (2026-10-20)", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23524358", "publication_date": "2026-10-21", "description": "<p>This expanded archival research collection brings together the Baird / ZoraASI corpus and Jennifer Lorraine Nielsen&rsquo;s separately authored gauge-gravity preprint, with recent research papers, computational records, reproducibility audits and supporting materials.</p>\n<p>The public reading edition contains 9,252 pages: four new editorial pages, the reviewed 7,399-page public baseline, and a 1,849-page research supplement. The supplement contains 550 byte-distinct existing PDFs dated 19 September through 20 October 2026, plus a verbatim PDF rendering of the 20 October free-bath reference report. Identical file copies were removed; historical repetitions and distinct revisions may remain.</p>\n<p>The ZIP supplies original supplemental PDFs, available authoring sources, the current report&rsquo;s code and numerical results, a detailed catalogue, physical page maps, SHA-256 checksums and assembly/verification tools. Its scope is the locally identified baseline and documented research folders. The main PDF and catalogue are also supplied separately for convenient reading.</p>\n<p>Nielsen&rsquo;s included 116-page preprint is The Complex Hopf Fibration as the Canonical Space for Gauge-Gravity Unification: The Field, Universal Action, and Particle Spectrum, Preprints.org v5 (17 July 2026), DOI 10.20944/preprints202604.0315.v5, CC BY 4.0. Her authorship and notices are retained. Only this publicly licensed preprint is reproduced; the 240-page manuscript without a stated reuse license and the personal study guide are excluded. Inclusion does not assert her coauthorship of the Baird corpus or endorsement of the compilation.</p>\n<p>This is a research archive, not a declaration of a completed or experimentally validated Theory of Everything. Claims retain their source statuses, assumptions and corrections. File integrity and page fidelity checks do not constitute scientific validation. Rights remain component-specific; see RIGHTS_AND_ATTRIBUTION.txt.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Baird, Christopher Michael", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["Theory of everything", "MQGT-SCF", "ZoraASI", "research corpus", "Hopf fibration", "reproducibility", "Hadamard matrices", "research archive"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.20944/preprints202604.0315.v5", "relation": "hasPart", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://philarchive.org/rec/NIETTU", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "url"}], "dates": [{"type": "copyrighted", "description": "\"Unifying the Universe: A Comprehensive Guide to the Theory of Everything\""}], "version": "2026.10.20", "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/Cbaird26/mqgt-scf-continued/tree/edition/2026-10-20-expanded-public"}, "resource_type": {"title": "Other", "type": "publication", "subtype": "other"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 306, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "14019809"}}]}}, "title": "A Theory of Everything \u2014 Expanded Research Collection: Baird / ZoraASI Corpus, Nielsen Preprint, and Research Supplements (2026-10-20)", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23524358", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23524358", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23524358?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23524358", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/